{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of its height overwhelming the roof eaves level of the host dwellinghouse, a lack of a setback from the side boundary and its piecemeal design form, would result in an incongruous and overbearing additions to the dwellinghouse on a prominent corner site that overwhelms the architectural character host dwelling and causes harm to the character and openness of the streetscene, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy CS1.B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and the London Borough of Harrow’s Residential Design Guide Supplementary Planning Document (2010).&nbsp;",
    "The submitted Flood Risk Assessment is insufficient as it fails to adequately address the potential displacement of flood waters arising from the proposed development, and does not provide clear evidence to demonstrate the availability or suitability of compensatory flood storage on site, contrary to the requirements of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy SI 12 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CS1 of the Harrow Core Strategy (2010) and Policies DM9 and DM10 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013)."
  ],
